   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishing a single window system for the facilitation of economic activity in free economic zones in Tajikistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In a letter dated December 25, 2023 [#10/2-977], H.E. Mr. Zavqizoda Zavqi Amin, the Minister of Economic Development and Trade of the Republic of Tajikistan (MEDT), requested UNIDO#s technical assistance to support the digital transformation of Tajikistan&apos;s national economy. Following consultations with representatives of MEDT, UNIDO explored opportunities for technical assistance to strengthen the national digital innovation and entrepreneurial ecosystems, aligning with the Country#s strategic plans for developing the digital economy.  UNIDO developed the current project aimed at supporting the implementation of the 2030 National Development Strategy and the Mid-Ter m Program for the Development of the Digital Economy in Tajikistan for 2021#2025, bolstering the Government of Tajikistan&apos;s digital transformation efforts by focusing on two main areas (1) Free economic zones (FEZ), industrial clusters, and SMEs in target sectors; (2) Key public sector initiatives to facilitate technology and knowledge transfer, enhancing public sector efficiency, increasing SME productivity and international competitiveness, and fostering a digital and innovation-driven entrepreneurial ecosystem. The project seeks to facilitate the integration of Tajikistan into the wider Eurasian economic landscape, leveraging reinforced linkages</narrative>
  </description>
